ngs_growth":0.097,"shares_outstanding":110720000.0,"float_shares":46118662.0,"held_pct_insiders":0.58324003,"held_pct_institutions":0.20771,"beta":0.258,"fifty_two_week_high":1884.0,"fifty_two_week_low":1365.0,"fifty_day_average":1577.136,"two_hundred_day_avg":1610.2905,"target_high_price":2015.0,"target_low_price":1509.0,"target_mean_price":1751.6666,"recommendation":"none","num_analyst_opinions":3,"all_time_high":2960.0,"all_time_low":34.8,"long_business_summary":"Grindwell Norton Limited manufactures and sells abrasives, ceramics, and plastic products in India and internationally. It operates through Abrasives, Ceramics & Plastics, Digital Services, and Others segments. The company offers abrasives, including bonded and coated abrasives, non-woven abrasives, thin wheels, construction products, automotive aftermarket, adhesives and sealants, performance grinding products; life science solutions, such as biopharmaceutical systems, medical components, cell therapy solutions, and industrial and consumer solutions; and performance polymer solutions, including engineered components, tape solutions, and ADFORS. It also provides performance ceramics and refractories solutions comprising ceramic systems, wear resistance technology, specialty ceramic for energy, iron and steel, foundry, and non-ferrous industries; silicon carbide crude and grains, including ceramic foam filters for metallurgy, crucible, abrasive, refractory, and advanced materials applications; and design and commissioning solutions. The company serves construction and mobility industries. Grindwell Norton Limited was founded in 1941 and is based in Mumbai, India. Grindwell Norton Limited (BSE:506076) operates as a subsidiary of Compagnie de Saint-Gobain S.A."}}